  "text": "Question twelve. Why compute ratios from summed components instead of averaging per-row ratios? Because an average of ratios weighs every row the same. One day has a single order for two hundred dollars. The next has ten thousand orders worth five hundred thousand. Average the two days' order values, and you get a hundred twenty-five dollars. Sum the revenue, sum the orders, then divide: just over fifty dollars, which is what the average order really was. So a model keeps the numerator and the denominator, and divides at whatever grain the report asks for.",
